{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwjENNCzSgVEDi8xV8RF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't confirmed that the rule fires, and I haven't opened the dashboard to check how the panels render.\n\n**What the data holds:** The index has one document per web request. Key fields:\n- `timestamp`\n- `response` (a string status code)\n- `bytes`\n- `extension`\n- `clientip`\n- `geo.src` and `geo.dest`\n- `machine.os`\n- `url`\n- `host`\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-4dc49203 Web logs overview\" has four panels and defaults to the last 7 days.\n- **Total requests:** a single count.\n- **Requests over time:** a line chart on `timestamp`.\n- **Responses by status code:** a pie chart on `response.keyword`.\n- **Average bytes by extension:** a bar chart on `extension.keyword`.\n- **Link:** http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-4dc49203-web-logs-overview-50b9e2aa82d2\n\n**Alert rule:** \"EFF-4dc49203 5xx spike\" is an Elasticsearch query rule that runs every minute.\n- **Condition:** it counts documents whose `response.keyword` starts with \"5\" over a 5-minute window and fires when the count is above 10.\n- **Status:** right after creation its status was \"pending\", because it hadn't run yet.\n- **Actions:** it has no actions attached, so a firing only shows up as an alert in Kibana and doesn't notify anyone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1290,"cache_read_input_tokens":19085,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1290},"output_tokens":505,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"bd40ab5c-c725-40b7-a9e3-914a7209139c","tim